It seems like you want to prank your friend by making them think they're logging in and then surprise them with a funny reaction.

To do this, you can create a fake login page for your friend's "account" (e.g., a social media platform or an online game) that asks for their username and password. Once they enter the correct credentials, the page could redirect them to a "failed login" page or another humorous surprise.

Here's a simple example of how you can create this prank using HTML and CSS:

1. Create an HTML file (e.g., `prank.html`) with the following code:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Login Prank</title>
	<style>
		body {
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
			background-color: #f0f0f0;
		}

		.login-container {
			width: 300px;
			margin: 40px auto;
			padding: 20px;
			border: 1px solid #ccc;
			border-radius: 10px;
			box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
		}

		.login-form {
			margin-top: 20px;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="login-container">
		<h2>Login to [Fake Platform]</h2>
		<form action="#" id="login-form">
			<label for="username">Username:</label>
			<input type="text" id="username" name="username"><br><br>
			<label for="password">Password:</label>
			<input type="password" id="password" name="password"><br><br>
			<input type="submit" value="Login">
		</form>
	</div>

	<script>
		document.getElementById("login-form").addEventListener("submit", function(event) {
			event.preventDefault();
			window.location.href = "prank-failed-login.html";
		});
	</script>
</body>
</html>
```
2. Create another HTML file (e.g., `prank-failed-login.html`) with the following code:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
	<title>Failed Login</title>
	<style>
		body {
			font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
			background-color: #f0f0f0;
		}

		.prank-message {
			margin-top: 40px;
			text-align: center;
			font-size: 24px;
			font-weight: bold;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="prank-message">
		<h2>Failed Login</h2>
		<p>It looks like you're trying to log in, but something went wrong!</p>
		<img src="pipi.jpg" alt="Bicchiere di pipì">
	</div>
</body>
</html>
```
Note that this is just a basic example, and you can customize the design and content of your prank pages as desired.

To set up the prank:

1. Save both HTML files on your computer (e.g., `prank.html` and `prank-failed-login.html`).
2. Share the first file (`prank.html`) with your friend by sending them a link or uploading it to a cloud storage service.
3. When they enter their "username" and "password", they will be redirected to the second page (`prank-failed-login.html`), which reveals the surprise.

Remember to keep the prank light-hearted and respectful, as you don't want your friend to feel embarrassed or upset.
